Send a login fingerprint so two-factor authentication works

Discord now rejects every 2FA code unless the login and the /auth/mfa/totp
request carry an X-Fingerprint obtained from /auth/fingerprint; a rejected
attempt can also sign the account out everywhere. This is the cause of
purple-discord issues #477 and #489, and the same fix Discord Lite made in
dosdude1/discord-lite@fde55a8.

- Fetch /auth/fingerprint before the password login and send it (with a
  login Referer) on the unauthenticated requests.
- Send the same login and 2FA bodies as the official client
  (undelete, login_source, gift_code_sku_id).
- Report Discord's own error message (eg. "Invalid two-factor code") instead
  of "Bad username/password".
- Free fingerprint and mfa_ticket on close.

